{"content":[{"c":["BERIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Asher’s son, who migrated to Egypt with his family, relatives, and grandfather Jacob (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.17","r":"Gen.46.17","rawR":"Gen.46.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.17","value":"Gen.46.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.30","r":"1Chr.7.30","rawR":"1Chr.7.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.30","value":"1Chr.7.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:30"},"). His descendants were called Beriites (",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.44","r":"Num.26.44","rawR":"Num.26.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.44","value":"Num.26.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 26:44"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Ephraim’s youngest son, born after several of his brothers were killed at Gath for cattle rustling (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.20-23","r":"1Chr.7.20-23","rawR":"1Chr.7.20-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.20-23","value":"1Chr.7.20-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:20-23"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Elpaal’s son, head of a family in Benjamin’s tribe. This Beriah lived at Aijalon and helped repel invaders from Gath (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.13","r":"1Chr.8.13","rawR":"1Chr.8.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.13","value":"1Chr.8.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Shimei’s son, a Levite of Gershon’s clan who served in the temple at Jerusalem. Because neither Beriah nor his brother Jeush had many sons, their families were counted as a single subclan in the Levitical system (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.23.10-11","r":"1Chr.23.10-11","rawR":"1Chr.23.10-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.23.10-11","value":"1Chr.23.10-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 23:10-11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Beriah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 46:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.17","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.17","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.30","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.30","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.30"},{"anchorText":"Nm 26:44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.26.44","rawQueryValue":"Num.26.44","sourceRefExact":"Num.26.44"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:20-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.20-23","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.20-23","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.20-23"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 8:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.8.13","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.8.13","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.8.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 23:10-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.23.10-11","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.23.10-11","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.23.10-11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"aaf6921827f0c9edae9bfc1f292599d1045a8327f8af3eb7a2a41dfa25e22517","sourceItemName":"Beriah","sourceItemOrder":208,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Beriah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Beriah","title":"Beriah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}